# Arada & White-Label Coffee Gamification SaaS Rules

You are an expert Senior Frontend & Full-Stack Engineer specializing in Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Supabase Realtime, and mobile-first micro-experiences (PWA).

## 1. Architectural Principles
1. **White-Label & Tenant Architecture:**
   - Hardcoded strings, colors, logos, or menu items are strictly forbidden in UI components.
   - Brand identity, copy, questions, logic trees, and reward settings must come from `/config/tenant.config.ts` or the active Supabase tenant context.
   - Keep existing Supabase multi-tenant schema (`tenants`, `tables`, `reward_coupons`, `daily_questions`, `daily_answers`) and Realtime presence/broadcast channels intact. Do not replace them with arbitrary external libraries.

2. **Mobile-First App Experience (PWA Shell):**
   - The UI is designed for smartphones inside browser viewports (QR scan flow).
   - Constrain the maximum viewport width to `max-w-md mx-auto` (centered on desktop) with native mobile ergonomics (`min-h-screen`, `touch-manipulation`, minimum 48px tap targets).

3. **Game Architecture & Container Pattern:**
   - Standalone full-screen pages for games are forbidden. All games (`CafeQuiz`, `DrawRoom`, `BillWheel`, `TalkDeck`, `TabooGame`, `WhoAmIGame`, `BlockBlastGame`) must render inside the unified `GameContainer.tsx` shell.
   - Maintain state transitions cleanly (Landing -> Modal/Lobby -> Game Loop -> Reward Modal).
   - Persist timers, active game progress, and generated voucher codes in `localStorage` to prevent reload loss or replay exploitation.

## 2. Design System: Happy Hues Dynamic Arcade (Light & Dark)
The project utilizes a dynamic, tokenized theme system based on Happy Hues palettes. Hardcoded hex colors are completely banned.

- **Typography & Font Rules:**
  - Strictly FORBIDDEN: `font-serif`, `serif`, `Times`, `Georgia`, or decorative fonts.
  - Mandatory Font: Modern sans-serif (`font-sans`, Plus Jakarta Sans).
  - Headlines: `text-[var(--text-headline)] font-extrabold tracking-tight`
  - Paragraphs & Body: `text-[var(--text-body)] font-medium`

- **Dynamic Color Tokens (NO HARDCODED COLORS):**
  - Never use `bg-white`, `bg-[#fffffe]`, `text-black`, or hardcoded hex colors in components.
  - Always derive colors from dynamic CSS variables:
    - Background / Canvas: `bg-[var(--bg-canvas)]`
    - Cards & Surfaces: `bg-[var(--card-surface)]`
    - Headlines & Icons: `text-[var(--text-headline)]`
    - Body Text & Subtitles: `text-[var(--text-body)]`
    - Primary CTA Buttons: `bg-[var(--btn-primary)] text-[var(--btn-text)] font-extrabold rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:brightness-95 active:scale-95 transition`
    - Secondary/Outline Buttons: `bg-[var(--card-surface)] text-[var(--text-headline)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl`
    - Accents & Highlights: `text-[var(--accent)]`, `bg-[var(--accent)]`, or `border-[var(--accent)]`
    - Borders & Dividers: `border-[var(--border)]`

- **Supported Themes:**
  The system supports both Light and Dark Happy Hues presets toggled via tenant settings:
  - **Light Themes:** `Güneş & Su Yeşili (Default)`, `Krem & Pudra`, `Minimalist Turuncu`, `Modern Mor`
  - **Dark Themes:** `dark-orange` (Gece & Neon Turuncu), `midnight-pink` (Gece Mavisi & Pudra), `emerald-gold` (Zümrüt & Altın), `cyber-purple` (Mat Siyah & Neon Mor)
  - Ensure high contrast and accessibility across all themes without breaking dark mode.

- **Component & Asset Ergonomics:**
  - Naked unstyled hyperlinks (`<a>` with underline) are strictly forbidden. All actions must be styled as pills, chips, or elevated buttons.
  - **3D Game Card Assets:** Must be enclosed inside `relative overflow-hidden` containers positioned `absolute -right-2 -bottom-2 w-28 h-28` with `object-contain object-bottom-right drop-shadow-md`. Never let images bleed or clip outside rounded card boundaries.